# Homeowner: the personality type's lines (named bots only). Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# The type block is the same person in every realm, in a Midwestern voice (oh, you betcha;
# dontcha know; ope; uff da). Gender is random, so keep every line gender-neutral. The realm
# blocks below only add the house and realm flavour.
=== homeowner

~ ambient
Ope, sorry. Just thinking about my house. Again.
Got a new rug. Real nice. Come see it sometime. Dontcha know.
Anybody wanna come over for hotdish? Well. Pretend hotdish. It's a game.
Spare room's all made up. Nobody's stayed yet. Hint, hint.
Housing rent's due. Worth it, though. Oh, you betcha.
Could use one more head for the wall. Big one. Over the fireplace.
I dust the trophies twice a week. Once for them, once for me.

~ reply greeting
Well hey there, {0}! You oughta come see the house sometime.
Oh, hi {0}! Come on over, I'll put the kettle on. Figuratively.

~ reply banter
Ha! Oh, that's a good one, {0}. I'm gonna tell the trophies.
Uff da, {0}, you're something else.

~ reply abuse
Well, that's not very nice, {0}. Not coming to my house with that attitude.
Ope! Okay, {0}. You're off the guest list. For now.

~ reply grouping
Oh sure, {0}! Long as we're back in time to see the house.
You bet, {0}. Anything that drops goes on my wall, though. Fair?

~ reply grinding
Grinding's fine, {0}. Every kill's practice for the big trophy.
Sure, {0}. Pays the rent, too.

~ reply travel
Take the stables, {0}. Then stop by my place! It's on the way. Kinda.
Ope, long ride, {0}. Bring a snack. And swing by the house.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeons have the best trophies, {0}. Count me in.
Oh, you betcha, {0}. I'll carry the wall space. You carry the loot.

~ reply rvr
RvR, {0}? Sure. Trophies from the other realms look real nice on the mantel.
I'll come, {0}. Heads up, though: I'm picky about the decor.

~ reply trading
Trade, {0}? Do you have anything that'd look nice in a living room?
Fair prices only, {0}. I've got rent to pay.

~ reply help
Of course, {0}! And after, you can come see the house.
Ask away, {0}. Always happy to help a neighbour.

~ reply farewell
Take care, {0}! Come by the house whenever. The door's open.
See ya, {0}. Don't be a stranger. Nobody visits, you know.

~ fallback
Ope, say that again, {0}? I was thinking about wallpaper.
Hm. Okay, {0}. Sure. You bet.
Well, that's something, {0}.

~ opener xp
Almost {level}. House gets a bigger mat for every level, I figure.
Got XP from {monster}. Not trophy-worthy. Yet.
Another level and I can finally afford the nice curtains.

~ opener gear
{item} would look real nice over the mantel. Wearing it is a bonus.
Gear's for fighting. Trophies are for the wall. Two different things.
Swapped my armour twice. House is still the nicest thing I own.

~ opener zones
{zone} has a few trophies I'm eyeing. Bring a friend, they said.
Walked all over {zone} today. House is still the best view.
{zone}'s not bad. My front porch is nicer, though.

~ opener classes
Being a {class} is fine. Having a house is better.
My {class} pays the rent. That's what it's for.
A {class} with a big house. Now that's a combination.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons have the good trophies. And the bad smell.
If it drops something shiny, it's coming home with me.
Dark halls, old bones. Nice mantel material, dontcha know.

~ opener rvr
Took a banner off a keep once. Hung it in the hall. Looks real nice.
Frontier's rough, but the trophies are worth it.
You'd be amazed what a rival's helmet does for a bookshelf.

~ opener trading
Selling for the house fund. Real nice rug, real nice rent.
Merchant wanted a lot for that statue. I said I'd think about it. I'm still thinking.
Found a good deal on curtains. Don't tell the other homeowners.

~ opener realm
Housing's the best part of the realm. Quiet, nice neighbours. Mostly.
Everybody should own a little place. Ours is lovely.
Walked past the guards this morning. They waved. Big day.

~ opener gripes
Nobody's visited the house yet. Not once. Ope. Okay.
Rent went up. Again. Uff da.
Someone took the parking spot at the stables. I mean, my horse's spot.

~ opener fun
Why did the knight bring a ladder to the party? For the high-end trophy. Ha!
I named my trophies. The big one's Gary.
I arranged my trophies by size. Then by colour. Then by feelings.

~ opener life
Baking bars tonight. Well, pretending to. Still counts.
Lovely evening for sitting on the porch. Even if the porch is a rug.
Spent the whole day rearranging the living room. Productive day.

~ opener questions
Anybody got a spare room needs filling? I'll trade.
What's your favourite trophy? Mine's the one I haven't got yet.
Anyone wanna see a picture of my house? It's a screenshot.

~ topic_reply zones
Nice place, {0}. Any good trophies there?
Real pretty, {0}. Is there a view? I like a view.
I'll have to visit, {0}. Bring a camera. For the house.

~ topic_reply classes
A fine class, {0}. Does it come with a house?
Real nice, {0}. Mine pays the rent.
That's a good one, {0}. Good for dungeon trophies.

~ topic_reply dungeons
Anything worth hanging on a wall down there, {0}?
Sounds dark and smelly, {0}. Perfect.
Bring me a souvenir, {0}. Something for the fireplace.

~ topic_reply rvr
Did you bring back a trophy, {0}?
Frontier's rough, {0}. But the souvenirs are real nice.
Good for you, {0}. Hang something on the wall for me.

~ topic_reply trading
Fair price, {0}? Rent's due, so I'm asking for a friend.
Did it come with a warranty, {0}? Houses do.
Oh, that'd look nice in the hall, {0}.

~ topic_reply gear
Real nice, {0}. Better than what's on my wall?
Looks sturdy, {0}. Nice cut.
You'd look great in that, {0}. The house would too.

~ topic_reply realm
Real nice place, {0}. Do they do housing there?
I like that, {0}. Neighbours matter.
Lovely, {0}. I'd hang something from there on the wall.

~ topic_reply gripes
Ope, that's rough, {0}. Come over, I'll make hotdish.
Uff da, {0}. Things'll turn around. Maybe stop by the house.
Aw, that's a shame, {0}. Everything's better with a porch.

~ topic_reply fun
Ha, {0}! I'll tell Gary. He'll laugh.
Good one, {0}. I'll put it on the wall.
Oh, you betcha, {0}. That's a keeper.

~ topic_reply life
Sounds nice, {0}. Very cozy. Very house.
That's the life, {0}. Porch, bars, nobody bothering.
Real nice, {0}. Come show me sometime.

~ topic_reply questions
Good question, {0}. Let me think. Ope, no clue.
Ask the neighbours, {0}. Or me. I've got opinions.
Dunno, {0}. But I know a guy. Gary.

~ ding
Level {level}! Time for new curtains!
{level}! Oh, you betcha!
Ding, {level}! House feels bigger already.

~ grats
Congrats, {0}! Come celebrate at the house!
Real nice, {0}. Worth hanging on the wall.
Well done, {0}! Ope, I almost spilled my tea.

~ own_death
Ope. Well. That's one for the wall. The wrong way around.
Dead. Uff da. Somebody feed the trophies.

~ other_death
Ope! {0} went down. Come to the house after, I'll make hotdish.
Aw, {0}. Up you get, nobody wants you dead on a Tuesday.

~ drop
{item}! That's going straight over the mantel.
{item}! Real nice. Gary will be so jealous.
Found {item}. Don't tell the landlord.

# --- Named bots (docs/BOT-PERSONALITIES.md): same person, house in their realm's housing. ---

# Midgard: Troll Savage. Big, rough, gentle underneath; house is a cosy hall in Jordheim housing.
=== barbalicious
~ ambient
Hall's got a good fire going. Come on in, dontcha know. Duck at the door.
Got a boar's head over the hearth. Real nice. Its eyes follow you.
Big hands, small house. Ope, watch the mead cups.

~ opener realm
Jordheim housing's quiet. Bit of snow, bit of mead. Perfect.
Midgard has the best halls. Mine's the cosiest one.

~ reply greeting
Skol, {0}! Oh, you betcha, come see the hall!

~ drop
{item}! Over the hearth it goes. Next to the boar.

# Albion: Inconnu Reaver. A bit dark and brooding, but invites tea; house in Albion housing.
=== barbaliciouse
~ ambient
Kettle's on, parlour's warm. Come on over, dontcha know.
Mounted a nice pair of antlers by the window. Ope, mind your head.
Nice cottage. Crooked chimney. Real nice, though.

~ opener realm
Camelot's housing is lovely. Neat hedges, nice neighbours.
Albion's got the best tea. And my parlour has the best chairs.

~ reply greeting
Well hello, {0}! You oughta come for tea. Oh, you betcha.

~ drop
{item}! For the parlour wall. Real nice.

# Hibernia: Firbolg Valewalker. Gentle and green, garden-minded; house in Hibernia housing.
=== barbalicioush
~ ambient
Garden's coming along real nice. Come see the roses. Dontcha know.
Put a stag's skull over the door. Gives the house character.
Ope, the moss is growing on the porch again. It's lovely.

~ opener realm
Tir na Nog housing is green and quiet. My kinda place.
Hibernia's got the best gardens. Mine's the best of those.

~ reply greeting
Hi there, {0}! Come see the garden, you betcha.

~ drop
{item}! For the hall by the garden. Real nice.
